# Managed by league repo -- do not edit deployed copy
# Source: league/server/crontab-main/league-maintenance.cron
# Deploy: yarn load:crontab:main  (scope league-main -> league:~/crontab/league-maintenance.cron)
#
# League

## Every Sunday at 4:00AM — verify named-catalog rows match DB config (replaces retired drift-detector slot)
0 4 * * 0 NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/verify-named-format-catalog.mjs >> /var/log/league/verify-named-format-catalog.log 2>&1

## Every Sunday at 4:15AM — verify every named format carries derived gamelog data for
## every season the base gamelogs cover. Catches a format silently dropping out of the
## generation set (the 2025 gap that blanked the default league's gamelogs). Runs after
## verify-named-format-catalog so catalog drift is reported first.
15 4 * * 0 NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/verify-format-data-coverage.mjs >> /var/log/league/verify-format-data-coverage.log 2>&1

## Every Sunday at 4:45AM — assert drive_seq numbering stays game-continuous: no
## drive_seq value may appear in both halves of a game. This defect class produces
## wrong numbers rather than missing ones, so exit codes and output freshness are
## blind to it; the check measures the invariant directly and signals only when a
## violation class exceeds its recorded baseline.
45 4 * * 0 NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/audit-drive-seq-coherence.mjs >> /var/log/league/audit-drive-seq-coherence.log 2>&1

## Every Sunday at 6:15AM — run the whole registered data-check registry
## (db/checks/registry.mjs). Replaces the retired route-share coverage audit,
## whose two conditions are now two rows in that registry.
##
## The slot is load-bearing, not arbitrary. It sits after every Sunday line in
## this file (4:00, 4:15, 4:45) and after the last daily 5:xx line (5:45), so
## nothing here grades data another job is still writing. The keeptradecut audit
## below records what the alternative costs: it ran 30 minutes too early for
## months and graded pre-import data. Grading mid-import manufactures exactly
## the false findings this system claims 100 percent accuracy over.
##
## A non-zero exit means a CHECK could not run — it crashed, its gradeable
## population collapsed below its floor, or its finding failed to reach the
## signal queue. Findings themselves ride self-closing signals and never turn
## this red.
15 6 * * 0 NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/run-data-checks.mjs >> /var/log/league/run-data-checks.log 2>&1

## Every day at 4:45AM
## Must run AFTER import-keeptradecut.mjs (4:30AM, league-imports.cron), which is
## the sole producer of the keeptradecut_valuations rows this reads. It ran at
## 4:00AM until 2026-08-02, so it never saw the current day's values; that was
## survivable only because a missing valuation was silently coerced to zero.
## The script now reports a day whose coverage collapses, so the ordering is
## load-bearing rather than cosmetic. 4:45 keeps it in its own slot in the
## keeptradecut morning chain (4:30 import, 4:45 here, 5:00 roster-asset-lineage,
## 5:15 calibrate-composite-market-value-sources, 5:45 generate-composite).
45 4 * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/calculate-team-daily-ktc-value.mjs >> /var/log/league/league-calculate-team-daily-ktc-value.log 2>&1

## Every day at 4:30AM
30 4 * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/generate-league-team-player-seasonlogs.mjs --all >> /var/log/league/league-generate-league-team-player-seasonlogs.log 2>&1

## Every day at 9:00AM -- coverage oracle for keeptradecut_liquidity. That table
## is collected once per calendar day and read by nothing, so a sustained
## collection loss has no other surface: the daily importer's pipeline_failure
## auto-resolves on the next morning's clean run, clearing the queue while the
## data gap persists. Grades through YESTERDAY only, so both liquidity recovery
## slots (12:30 and 20:30, league-imports.cron) have already had their chance at
## every day it counts. Fires only on 2+ CONSECUTIVE missing days -- a single
## missing day is what the recovery slots exist to absorb.
0 9 * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/audit-keeptradecut-liquidity-coverage.mjs >> /var/log/league/audit-keeptradecut-liquidity-coverage.log 2>&1

## Every Monday at 5:00AM (with optimal-lineup pass)
0 5 * * 1 NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/generate-league-team-player-seasonlogs.mjs --all --with-optimal >> /var/log/league/league-generate-league-team-player-seasonlogs-with-optimal.log 2>&1

## Every day at 5:00AM. Backstop only since 2026-08-03 -- refresh-roster-asset-lineage.mjs
## below now rebuilds a league within a minute of any change to the walker's inputs.
## This full sweep stays because the watcher's fingerprint covers only the eight
## tables walk-transactions.mjs reads today: a walker that gains an input without
## the fingerprint gaining it too would go stale silently, and this run reasserts
## canonical state regardless. Every run is a full per-league delete-and-rebuild
## inside one transaction; lid=1 takes 9-25s, dominated by the snapshot recompute.
0 5 * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/generate-roster-asset-lineage.mjs --all >> /var/log/league/league-generate-roster-asset-lineage.log 2>&1

## Every 5 minutes: rebuild any league whose lineage inputs changed. The lineage graph
## is read by the player_extended_salary data-view column, which renders a $0 salary
## for any player whose open holding still points at the pre-trade team -- so a graph
## that lags live activity serves wrong numbers rather than merely old ones.
## Fingerprints all eight walker input tables (22.8ms for lid=1) and no-ops when
## nothing moved; a changed fingerprint that writes 0 holdings is reported as failure.
##
## */5 rather than every minute because report_job writes an audit row per run
## regardless of outcome, and this job no-ops on almost all of them -- at 1/min it
## would add 1440 jobs rows a day, 5x the busiest existing job, to carry a latency
## win the reader cannot perceive: the data-view response it exists to correct is
## itself cached for 5 minutes. Matches the cadence class of every other frequent
## league job. Raise it only for a consumer that reads the graph directly and needs
## sub-5-minute freshness.
*/5 * * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/refresh-roster-asset-lineage.mjs >> /var/log/league/league-refresh-roster-asset-lineage.log 2>&1

## Calibrate composite market value sources (15 5 daily; 15-min buffer after FantasyPros draft import at 0 5 * 5-8 *)
15 5 * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/calibrate-composite-market-value-sources.mjs >> /var/log/league/calibrate-composite-market-value-sources.log 2>&1

## Generate composite market value daily (45 5; runs after calibration)
45 5 * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/generate-composite-market-value.mjs >> /var/log/league/generate-composite-market-value.log 2>&1

## Announce restricted free agent (check every 5 minutes, year-round; self-gating).
## NOT hour-pinned. The announcement schedule is derived from the league's own window
## configuration (restricted_free_agency_period_start + restricted_free_agency_window_hours),
## so a single daily slot cannot serve a sub-24h cadence — a 12-hour window announces twice
## a day and an hour-pinned cron would silently skip every second nomination. The script
## claims each window exactly once via the league_notifications unique constraint, so
## running it every 5 minutes is idempotent. This also removes the dependence on the host
## clock matching the league timezone.
*/5 * * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/announce-restricted-free-agent.mjs >> /var/log/league/announce-restricted-free-agent.log 2>&1

## Process restricted free agency bids (check every 5 minutes, year-round; self-gating).
## Same reasoning as above: each bid's processing time is derived from its own window and
## falls restricted_free_agency_processing_lead_hours before the next announcement, so
## processing always strictly precedes the next nomination. Bids not yet due are skipped.
*/5 * * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/process-restricted-free-agency-bids.mjs >> /var/log/league/process-restricted-free-agency-bids.log 2>&1

## Reset stale RFA tags (defense-in-depth) — daily at 5am, year-round. Idempotent: preserves any tag=4 backed by an un-cancelled current-year bid in restricted_free_agency_bids.
## NOT month-pinned. The window it guards moves with the offseason schedule: a Feb-May pin could not see the 2026 RFA window at all once it shifted to August, so the guard was dark for the one period it exists to cover. The script self-gates cheaply.
0 5 * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/reset-player-restricted-free-agency-tags.mjs >> /var/log/league/reset-player-restricted-free-agency-tags.log 2>&1

## Announce free agency period start (check every 30 minutes in August and September)
*/30 * * 8,9 * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/announce-free-agency-period-start.mjs >> /var/log/league/announce-free-agency-period-start.log 2>&1

## Process extensions at ext_date (check every 5 minutes, year-round; self-gating fires once per league per ext_date via league_notifications marker).
## NOT month-pinned. The deadline moves — a single-month pin (`5`) silently skipped the 2026 Jul-6 deadline and a 5-8 range would have skipped any shift past August. The gate is ext_date plus its 14-day auto-process retry tail (AUTO_PROCESS_WINDOW_DAYS in process-extensions.mjs), which the script evaluates itself in two cheap queries.
*/5 * * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/process-extensions.mjs >> /var/log/league/process-extensions.log 2>&1

## Expire protected practice squad designations at ext_date (check every 5 minutes, year-round). Same deadline as process-extensions above, so it runs at the same cadence; the two do not interact (extensions read active/reserve, this reads practice).
## NOT month-pinned, for the same reason the deadline moves. Needs no marker and no retry tail: the reset converges (PSP->PS, PSDP->PSD leaves nothing in scope), so a missed firing self-heals on the next one instead of expiring out of a window. Was scheduled NOWHERE until 2026-07-31 — it had run 4 times ever, all by hand, and league 1's 48 designations survived the 2026 deadline as a result.
*/5 * * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/reset-protected-designation.mjs >> /var/log/league/reset-protected-designation.log 2>&1

# League Each Season Week

## Generate the upcoming week's roster slice — daily at 23:55, year-round.
## NOT month-pinned, and NOT weekly. The job writes only the FUTURE slice (nextWeek = current week + 1), never the live one, so running it daily cannot clobber a manager's roster; it just bounds how stale that slice can get. Under the old `1,2,9-12` Monday pin the offseason week-1 slice was created in February and then frozen until September: in 2026 the last Monday reading week 0 fell on Aug 31, outside the month range, so the February snapshot — pre-draft, pre-auction, still carrying 2025 tags — would have gone live at kickoff and propagated into week 2.
55 23 * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/generate-rosters.mjs >> /var/log/league/league-generate-rosters.log 2>&1



# Maintenance

## Generate new season records (At 07:00 on the 1st, Feb through Aug - no-op until season-dates.mjs is updated)
0 7 1 2-8 * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/generate-seasons.mjs >> /var/log/league/generate-seasons.log 2>&1

## Create database partitions for upcoming season (At 00:00 on the 1st in May and July)
0 0 1 5,7 * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/create-season-partitions.mjs >> /var/log/league/create-season-partitions.log 2>&1

## Every day at 0:00
0 0 * * * job-wrapper.sh league-cleanup-puppeteer find /tmp -maxdepth 1 -name 'puppeteer*' -mtime +2 -exec rm -rf {} \; >> /var/log/league/league-cleanup-puppeteer.log 2>&1

## Check disk space every hour
0 * * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/check-disk-space-main-server.mjs >> /var/log/league/league-check-disk-space-main-server.log 2>&1

## Close rookie drafts whose window elapsed with picks unmade (hourly)
## Expires those picks per the 2023-09-03 ruling. Nothing else closes a draft
## that does not finish -- the draft route records completion only when the
## final pick is made -- so without this an abandoned pick stays a tradeable
## asset forever. Hourly rather than seasonal: the close is what makes a pick
## stop being tradeable, so the lag between window close and sweep is a window
## in which an expired pick can still be traded. Self-gates to one grouped
## query when no league has an outstanding pick past its deadline.
30 * * * * NODE_ENV=production /root/.nvm/versions/node/current/bin/node /root/league/scripts/close-expired-rookie-drafts.mjs >> /var/log/league/close-expired-rookie-drafts.log 2>&1



# Crontab Export

## Export crontab for backup sync (hourly)
0 * * * * crontab -l > /tmp/league-crontab.txt
